         ("He should choose thoroughly cooked meat, fish, shellfish, and eggs and avoid raw or half-cooked dishes", True, "Recipients are taught to eat thoroughly cooked meat, eggs, fish, and shellfish and to avoid kinilaw, raw oysters, and half-cooked egg."),
         ("He should avoid all food at the fiesta and bring only canned goods from home", False, "Total avoidance is unnecessary. Safe choices of cooked food are the practical teaching."),
